{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IntervalTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bound","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bound","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The intervals are kept in an AVL tree ordered by lower bound, then upper bound, then the order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were inserted in, and each vertex also records the largest upper bound in its subtree, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a search skips every subtree that ends before the query begins (Cormen, Leiserson, Rivest and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Stein, ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Introduction to Algorithms"}]},{"text":", §14.3). The same interval may be stored more than once,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with different values.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var meetings = IntervalTree<Int, String>()","meetings.insert(9 ..< 10, value: \"stand-up\")","meetings.insert(10 ..< 12, value: \"design review\")","meetings.insert(11 ..< 13, value: \"lunch\")","meetings.containing(11).map(\\.value)          \/\/ [\"design review\", \"lunch\"]","meetings.overlapping(9 ..< 11).map(\\.value)   \/\/ [\"stand-up\", \"design review\"]","meetings.contained(in: 9 ..< 12).map(\\.range) \/\/ [9 ..< 10, 10 ..< 12]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intervals are half-open, so "},{"code":"9 ..< 10","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"10 ..< 12","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" touch without overlapping. As a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection, the tree’s elements are its entries in that order, read by in-order position."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/ST"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/Entry","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/Iterator","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/SearchView"],"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/init()","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/init(checked:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/contained(in:)","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/containing(_:)","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/insert(_:value:)","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/insert(checke